Navigation Commands/Methods
===================================

To navigate between application we have in Selenium Navigation interface

Navigation interface provides 4 methods
----------------------------------
1.to(url): navigate to application 

driver.navigate().to(url)

2.back():Navigate back

driver.navigate().back()

3.forward(): Navigate forward

driver.navigate().forward()

4.refresh():To refresh webpage

driver.navigate().refresh()


============================================
How to automate any webelement
===================================
For web application any graphical user interface(GUI) is webelement
examples: textbox,checkbox,radiobutton,button,link.....etc

In Technical WebElement is an interface in Selenium

To automate any webelement 
-----------------------
1.Identify webelement address
2.Perform action on webelement

To identify weblement address we use in Selenium Locators

What is Locator?
--------------------
Locator is an address of webelement from webpage

Selenium Support total 8 locators
------------------------------------
1.By id (primary)
2.By name
3.By className
4.By tagName
5.By linkText
6.By partialLinkText

Dynamic locators
-----------------
7.By cssSelector
8.By xpath

